#: content/competitors.ts
msgid "Yes, and for the same three jobs. OpenShorts builds one image with a GPU flag: faster-whisper on CUDA, NVENC encoding, and its detection models. Reelsaw adds a Compose override (docker-compose.gpu.yml) that hands the card to the Speaches container (faster-whisper on CUDA with large-v3), to Ollama when it runs in a container, and to the app, whose ffmpeg then encodes with NVENC; its face, text and alignment models stay on the CPU by default because they are small enough that the GPU did not measure faster. Neither runs CUDA inside Docker on a Mac; there, Reelsaw's installer runs Ollama natively on Metal."
